        {
          "id": "b2da308b-18ac-4255-8bfe-4e76172099d8",
          "listId": "1c7b07a3-8aa4-4c54-93c7-4cea40d0df16",
          "title": "CORS Cache invalidation is too aggressive",
          "description": "When we make any change to a project key we clear the cache of the allowed origins for CORS. this is too aggressive and can cause performance issues if we have a lot of changes to the project keys.\n\nWe should edit the cache content instead of clearing it. so if we add a new origin we just add it to the cache and if we remove an origin we just remove it from the cache.\n",
          "labels": [
